      "title": "Troubleshooting Intermittent Failures and Browser Inconsistencies",
      "content_summary": "Guidance for handling tickets where users report slow responses, inconsistent browser behavior, or intermittent failures without a clear root cause.",
      "content_body": "First, verify that the customer's environment matches the officially supported configuration matrix. If the setup is unsupported, provide standard browser compatibility guidance and close as a configuration change. For persistent issues in supported environments, gather detailed HAR files and browser console logs to rule out network or extension conflicts. If initial triage reveals no obvious client-side errors, escalate to engineering with a request for backend log correlation. In cases where logs remain inconclusive after a week, mark the ticket as 'insufficient information' and request a screen recording to clarify the user's workflow."
